        en: 'A heat pump tumble dryer recovers heat through a closed loop and uses about 50% less electricity than a condenser dryer, which heats air with a simple element. It also dries at lower temperature, gentler on laundry, in exchange for a longer cycle. Over the lifespan, the energy saving easily offsets the higher purchase price.',
